==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Havsnejonöga.jpg|thumb|A '''lamprey''']]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|laumprei}}, adopted from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|lampreie}} (Modern ''[[lamproie]]''), from {{etyl|ML.|en}} ''[[lampreda]]'', possibly from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|lampetra}}, from a combination of {{m|la|lambō||lick}} + {{m|la|petra||stone}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlæm.pɹi/|/ˈlæm.pɹeɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-ca-lamprey.opus|Audio (CA)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|lam|prey|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any long slender [[primitive]] eel-like [[freshwater]] and saltwater [[fish]] of the [[Petromyzontidae]] [[family]], having a [[sucking]] [[mouth]] with [[rasping]] [[teeth]] but no [[jaw]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|brook lamprey}}
* {{l|en|European river lamprey}}
* {{l|en|sea lamprey}}

